# QA After Gameplay Changes (ABSOLUTE — ALWAYS ON)

**Mandatory.** The owner must not have to ask "did you run QA?" after combat, planning, sim, or ability work.

If this turn **changed gameplay systems** (see scope below), the agent **must run the matching automated QA suite(s)** and **report PASS or FAIL** in the turn **Changelog** before ending the turn. **Do not claim a fix is done without QA output.**

## What counts as a gameplay-system change

Any edit under these paths (or equivalent behavior owners):

| Domain | Typical paths / owners |
|--------|-------------------------|
| Simulation | `core/simulation/`, `Simulator`, `ResolutionPipeline`, `BoardState` / `UnitState` resolution |
| Combat systems | `core/systems/` (`AbilitySystem`, `MovementSystem`, `CombatSystem`, …) |
| Planning / commit | `presentation/combat_planning_input.gd`, `combat_director.gd`, commit slots, preview, drag/drop, undo |
| Abilities / data | `data/definitions/`, ability `.tres`, factories that affect combat legality or resolution |
| Presentation tied to sim | `tactical_unit_layer.gd`, `tactical_planning_overlay.gd`, planning cursor/icons when commit/preview semantics change |
| Tests that **fix** gameplay | Changing production code **and** tests together still requires running the suite |

**Not in scope (QA not required):** pure docs, `.cursor/rules`, menu/UI theming with no combat behavior, living-map/VFX-only slices (use phase visual gates from `phase-audit.mdc` instead).

## Which suite to run

| Change touches | Run (headless) |
|----------------|----------------|
| Planning, preview, commit, drag, undo, cursor, overlay paths, `CombatDirector` refresh | **Planning QA gate (Tier 3 only)** — `.\scripts\run_planning_qa_gate.ps1` **once**. Do **not** also run `run_planning_scene_acceptance.ps1` in the same turn. |
| Core sim / bridge / broad combat regression | **Full regression** — `.\scripts\run_regression_tests.ps1 -GodotPath "<godot.exe>"` |
| Both planning and core sim | **Planning QA gate** + **full regression** (two commands, one run each) |

**Tier 1/2 headless fixture suites are legacy and disabled** from the gate and from `bridge_test_runner` — do not run `PlanningQaGate.tscn`, `run_planning_qa_gate.gd`, or `run_drag_e2e_only.gd` as QA unless the owner explicitly requests `-IncludeLegacyTier12` archaeology.

When unsure, run **Planning QA gate** at minimum for anything in `presentation/combat_*` or planning input. Run **full regression** when `core/simulation/` or `ResolutionPipeline` changes.

**Run QA once per turn.** Re-run only if the suite **FAIL**s and you are fixing toward a new pass.

Authoritative checklist mapping: `docs/PLANNING_QA_GATE.md`.

## Agent workflow (every gameplay edit turn)

1. Implement the change.
2. **Run** the required suite(s) — agent executes the command; do not only tell the owner to run it.
3. **Changelog (mandatory):** under `### QA`, record:
   - Suite name(s) run
   - **Result:** `PASS` or `FAIL`
   - On FAIL: paste or summarize `[FAIL]` lines; **fix or stop** — do not hand-wave "should work"
4. **Commit** per `auto-commit-absolute.mdc` only after QA **PASS**, or after documenting FAIL with owner-approved deferral.

## Fail policy

- **FAIL → do not mark task complete.** Fix and re-run QA, or stop and report blockers.
- **Skipped QA → rule violation** (same severity as skipping auto-commit).
- **Manual Layer B** (F5 pixels, walk anim feel, FPS) remains the owner's job; headless PASS does not replace visual checks for animation/perf claims.

## Relationship to other rules

- **Parent:** `global-systems-first.mdc` — preview/commit parity tests live in planning QA.
- **Complements:** `phase-audit.mdc` (phase gates), `move-preview-intent-truth.mdc` (drag E2E catches release path).
- **Wins over:** convenience, "small fix", ending the turn without running tests.
